# Copy to .env and fill in. Vite only exposes variables that start with VITE_.
VITE_ATS_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8000
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Not Vite's: scripts/corpus.ts reads a GitHub token for the corpus from its environment, never
# from this file, when gh is not logged in, as in CI. Never give either the VITE_ prefix.
# GH_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Not Vite's either: the naming model's key, one line with no spaces, a SoCLaaS key (clsk_...)
# from https://soclaas-portal.comp.nus.edu.sg (decision 0036), the one name all of its readers take.
# The dev server's naming route, /v1/name (scripts/serve-naming.ts), reads it from this file or the
# environment, on the server side alone, and asks the model for what its cache does not hold; with
# none it serves the cache alone, and the dev server says so when it starts. The Pages Function
# reads it from its own environment (functions/README.md). `corpus name --model`, `corpus run
# --allow-model` and `corpus bench --model <id>` (decision 0044) read it from their environment,
# never from this file (`set -a && source apps/editor/.env && set +a` loads it), and ask the model
# only when given that flag, never in CI.
# NAMING_MODEL picks the model by its SoCLaaS id, qwen3.8:27b when unset, for all of them; the
# model's answers go in .corpus/cache/<id>/, which `corpus review` reads, and `corpus run` unless
# --committed-only. Never give either the VITE_ prefix, which would put the key in the page.
# SOCLAAS_API_KEY=
# NAMING_MODEL=
